  <li><strong>August 16, 2026 &middot; Exhibit A &sect;42, &sect;8, &sect;69.2:</strong> Added a file-completion consequence framework for commissions that remain unclaimed or files that remain incomplete after closing. Superseded by the August 18, 2026 entry below; the current file-completion regime is set forth in the current text of Exhibit A &sect;42 and consists of capped administrative fees and a single percentage fee for late closing documentation, assessed against commission proceeds rather than retained from them. The rule that a commission, once earned, is not un-earned by later conduct remains governed by the Commission Structure Addendum Section 23 and Section 7.</li>
